  "Question": "The average of the numbers \\(1,\\) \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(\\cdots,\\) \\(98,\\) \\(99,\\) and \\(x\\) is \\(100x.\\) What is \\(x?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{49}{101}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{50}{101}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{51}{101}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{50}{99}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Pair the integers from opposite ends: \\(1+99=100\\), \\(2+98=100\\), and so on through \\(49+51=100\\). These are \\(49\\) pairs, with \\(50\\) left in the middle. Every integer from \\(1\\) through \\(99\\) is used exactly once, so\n\\[1+2+\\cdots+99=49\\cdot100+50=4950.\\]\nIncluding \\(x\\), there are \\(100\\) numbers. Their sum equals their average times their count, giving\n\\[4950+x=100(100x)=10000x.\\]\nSubtracting \\(x\\) yields \\(9999x=4950\\), and therefore\n\\[x=\\frac{4950}{9999}=\\frac{99\\cdot50}{99\\cdot101}=\\boxed{\\frac{50}{101}}.\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
